From 17d0b7205cf6eba2325fde8786a7d72c290259e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lilith River <lilith@imazen.io>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:27:54 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Don't treat an empty out-of-order jxlp box as end of input
 (#956)

* fix: don't treat an empty out-of-order jxlp box as end of input

`injected_jxlp` returned a buffered out-of-order `jxlp` box without
checking whether it still had bytes left. `CodestreamInput::read` then read
an empty slice and returned `Ok(0)`, and `available_bytes` returned `0`.
Callers take a 0-byte read as end of input (`SmallBuffer::refill` and
`fill_sections` both break on `num == 0`), so decoding stopped mid-frame
with codestream still buffered, surfacing as "Source file truncated".

`cjxl --output_mode=2` writes the DC group `jxlp` slots of a modular frame
with zero payload, one per DC group. With three DC groups the run of empty
boxes is short enough that the caller's retry path survives it; with four
or more it is not, so lossless files with 4+ DC groups (6145x256, but not
6144x256) failed to decode. Lossy frames put real data in those slots and
were unaffected.

Skip exhausted and empty buffered boxes in `injected_jxlp`, which covers
`read`, `available_bytes` and `skip` together since all three go through
it. `check_ooo_jxlp_done` removes the box it advances past, so the loop
terminates.

Adds a regression test that builds the container in memory and so needs no
fixture; without the fix it reads back a truncated codestream.

* test: move the regression to a test file and the standard harness

Replaces the hand-built container test with
`resources/test/ooo_jxlp_empty_dc_group_boxes.jxl` (878 bytes) and a
`declare_test_file!` entry, per review.

The file is 6145x1 lossless, written by `cjxl 0.12.0 -q 100 -e 7
--output_mode=2`. 6145 px is four 2048 px DC group columns, which is the
smallest shape that reproduces: a modular frame has no DC data, so the
container carries one empty `jxlp` box per DC group, and four consecutive
empty boxes are enough to exhaust the caller's retry path. At 6144 px the
frame has three DC groups and decodes even without the fix.

All nine generated tests fail without the fix and pass with it, including
`test_decode_test_file_chunks_*`, which feeds the file one byte at a time.

Local backport scope: production changes only. Upstream regression tests,
fixtures, and test-only harness changes are intentionally omitted. The
original commit message above describes the full upstream change.

diff --git a/jxl/src/api/inner/box_parser.rs b/jxl/src/api/inner/box_parser.rs
index 0f2485c9a..98e1882bc 100644
--- a/jxl/src/api/inner/box_parser.rs
+++ b/jxl/src/api/inner/box_parser.rs
@@ -289,6 +289,16 @@ impl BoxParser {
     }
 
     fn injected_jxlp(&mut self) -> Option<&mut OOOJxlpBox> {
+        // Skip 0-sized jxlp boxes.
+        while matches!(self.state, ParseState::BoxNeeded(_) | ParseState::Complete)
+            && let CodestreamBoxType::Jxlp(j, _) = self.latest_codestream_box
+            && self
+                .ooo_jxlp_buffer
+                .get(&j)
+                .is_some_and(|b| b.consumed == b.data.len())
+        {
+            self.check_ooo_jxlp_done();
+        }
         if matches!(self.state, ParseState::BoxNeeded(_) | ParseState::Complete)
             && let CodestreamBoxType::Jxlp(j, _) = self.latest_codestream_box
             && let Some(b) = self.ooo_jxlp_buffer.get_mut(&j)
